Yes. There are some excellent ways to automate Etsy listing media cheaply, especially for OddHobb. The biggest opportunity is combining your actual 3D meshes with reusable image templates, automated product videos, and AI-generated backgrounds.

You don't need to generate every listing image with AI. In fact, the cheaper, more consistent approach is to generate the creative elements once, then programmatically assemble hundreds of product images.

## 1. Etsy's current listing media limits (October 2026)

| Media            | Etsy accepts                        | My recommendation            |
| ---------------- | ----------------------------------- | ---------------------------- |
| Photos           | Up to 20 per listing                | 8–12 strong images initially |
| Videos           | Up to 2 per listing                 | Use both where useful        |
| Video duration   | Etsy pages differ: 3–15 or 5–15 sec | 5–15 seconds                 |
| Video formats    | MP4, MOV, FLV, AAC, AVI, 3GP, MPEG  | MP4, H.264                   |
| Video size       | Maximum 100 MB                      | Under 20 MB                  |
| Resolution       | Minimum 500 px; ideally 1080+       | 1080p                        |
| Sound            | Removed automatically               | Design for silent playback   |
| Photo formats    | JPG, PNG, GIF, SVG, HEIC            | JPG                          |
| Photo resolution | 2000 px or greater recommended      | 2000 × 2000 or 2500 × 2000   |

Etsy's updated listing guide confirms 20 photos and two videos. Its separate video guide gives slightly different minimum duration guidance, hence the safe 5–15-second recommendation.&#x20;

