I'd make the entire generator accept a single product manifest, for example:

```
{
  "sku": "ODD-PET-001",
  "mesh": "pet.glb",
  "photos": ["original.jpg"],
  "size_mm": [120, 85, 90],
  "material": "Full-colour printed material",
  "templates": [
    "white-hero",
    "gift-lifestyle",
    "size-guide",
    "photo-to-product",
    "turntable-video"
  ]
}
```

The generator would produce finished files, plus a manifest of exactly which inputs, prompts, templates and mesh versions produced each asset.

One important compliance point: Etsy requires original product media for seller-made items and disclosure when the item itself is AI-created. For personalised listings, the first image must show a finished customised example rather than an empty placeholder.&#x20;

