What I'd implement first: Batchroom-style image preparation, headless Blender rendering, and a small Remotion template collection. That gives OddHobb repeatable, cheap, brand-consistent listing packs immediately. Add expensive AI video only when there's a specific animation you cannot make from the actual mesh.

The bigger opportunity is treating listing templates as reusable product assets: one strong Christmas-card creative format can be reused for hundreds of customers, with only their photograph, message and artwork changing.